s through mid-October put her ahead by one to four points, though every recent survey comes from Republican-leaning pollsters.\n\nDemocrat Annie Andrews has run a serious campaign, outraising Graham roughly ten to one and drawing help from a favorable national midterm environment. Even so, the state's fundamentals, an expert consensus split between Lean R and Likely R, and prediction markets pricing Andrews around a one-in-five chance all point in the same direction. Graham is positioned to win by a mid-single-digit margin, with enough residual uncertainty that a strong closing stretch could narrow the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1565, "margin": -5.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2122, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2115, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2143, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1474, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2135, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2708, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2623, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2878, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2627, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2566, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.194, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2084, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1997, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2291, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2418, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.192, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.223, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.2237, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.2155, "margin": -4.0}, {"dat